# the pinned grammar versions in Cargo.toml are the contract; the
# lockfile is a build by-product here, not a distributed artifact
Cargo.lock
target/
# the twenty-three samples are fixtures for the probe, not files of this
# repository. One of them, flow.hs (the Haskell slot-table sample of plan
# v2.31 step 7, cited by core/app/CE/Lang/Haskell.hs), has no grammar arm
# in this probe: tsprobe pins no Haskell grammar, and that sample's kinds
# are checked against the node-types.json of the tree-sitter-haskell
# cli/Cargo.toml pins; it sits here beside the other flow samples. They stay tracked (`git add -f`); this pattern is what
# keeps them out of ce's two walks, which read .gitignore PATTERNS and
# never the index — so they enter neither the scan nor the advisory's
# mention universe (the universe formula counts them under
# pattern-ignored, the zod corpus precedent; a .ceignore is refused).
snippets/
